wer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d4f703-9f1b-5e6f-b25a-56dd0791a817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425592} {:answer/id #uuid "edf7d37e-5d75-5f27-bc9f-0079cc8b3b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edf7d37e-5d75-5f27-bc9f-0079cc8b3b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425633} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f9f671-11c9-5940-b954-9ff8e3b7a115" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4b9a1ad-55e6-52d3-8f59-ef1cc199427a" :question/math-academy-id "q-342459" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & x\\in [-3,0) \\\\ {x}^{2}, & x\\in [0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/11/11f9718c9384ad2fea0bf3f5cc7da720559c512a5b3cebbc11ca966d5ec0f28b.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}2x=2(-3)=-6\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}{x}^{2}=(3)^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement III is false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/d0/d0212ece76aba288e88b0c4d9f2e0f6163f4fd1f594cee30e9ea5f764ebc5f69.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113f0528-6296-5edc-a471-87b1ca2ca4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425554} {:answer/id #uuid "7686472d-41c3-5025-a423-4ae9721b5993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "113f0528-6296-5edc-a471-87b1ca2ca4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425554} :answer-field/id #uuid "08ecb117-6c45-5463-b318-8c285506eabc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76b55157-f226-54be-8fd3-e576ce7da945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425598} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0e6216-87df-59a6-808e-871e310b9484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce0e6216-87df-59a6-808e-871e310b9484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425623} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b521d38-d990-5b0d-80fe-d03ebd685a00" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e34f35d-c327-5601-b6ee-eb5051e0fda7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425561} {:answer/id #uuid "a698678d-21d8-5a48-b894-3c49a5fac693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a698678d-21d8-5a48-b894-3c49a5fac693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425612} :answer-field/id #uuid "60253eb4-3e5a-59a0-8c20-7c861c025f6e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "151f3b2c-1198-5804-bb25-a1fa989b21a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425557} {:answer/id #uuid "64cf008c-66db-51cd-bdbe-6511859f628e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "151f3b2c-1198-5804-bb25-a1fa989b21a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425557} :answer-field/id #uuid "a102f1e0-40e5-5ef6-a7de-a0e753751c70" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b957da1-0df2-5626-98d6-1a7c5a3632dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-342601" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{3}+3, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ x+1, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/2d/2d30d760181c95dd0764b9959ca91febb34e94618bb147d8022dae5745c38a1a.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}((x+2)^{3}+3)=(0)^{3}+3=3\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(x+1)=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement I is false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fcdf5654322a6deff9d7598590b4e0e1ace6150020b4944ad844976fb0f70230.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}