text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425608} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b76d48-4379-5b0c-bd2d-223ce4c993fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "311b1696-0203-596a-b731-cff98fe91a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425571} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4d884b0-d058-5f44-82e3-a0072396491a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa5cac21-63bb-59e7-aa34-0b7a399b8755" :question/math-academy-id "q-343062" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $8$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4$ defined on $[-4,4).$  Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $8$-periodic extension of $G(x)=x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4∼\\frac{20}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is  \n{{field-2}}\nand  \n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\nx∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=4.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{20}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that  \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-4,4),$\n\n- continuous on $[-4,4),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-4)=F(4),$ if we extend the value at $x=4$ using the formula $F(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4.$\n\nTherefore, the $8$-periodic extension $f$ is\n$\\text{continuous}$ and\n$\\text{piecewise smooth}$\non $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\,(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4) & ∼\\frac{d}{dx}\\,(\\frac{20}{3})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})) \\\\ x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}(-\\frac{n\\pi }{4}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})) \\\\ x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4}) \\\\ x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317372 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2e37d37-007c-569b-a44c-cb6a9d075371" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "102c20a7-364b-5e1d-8e5b-1a8f7adb1463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315216} {:answer/id #uuid "8f4a5b80-b993-5acb-b1fc-0027ff1b76db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315921} {:answer/id #uuid "9bfc4594-abfa-5c41-b497-cf307852b689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f4a5b80-b993-5acb-b1fc-0027ff1b76db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315921} :answer-field/id #uuid "5244a3bb-594f-53ba-b2ef-f72d466a2fc7" :answer-field/key "field-2"