92186425629} {:answer/id #uuid "fa872a28-3d62-5bdb-817b-84e0219ef7f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e698d1ad-201e-53de-8029-7a234688dc21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425629} :answer-field/id #uuid "e973ecec-8364-5900-9b48-eecc739a0ce6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9666624-6b3b-5d5b-bd5e-3f9ae5e53130" :question/math-academy-id "q-343337" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=6x$ defined on $[-3,3).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $6$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=3{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n6x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{36(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{36(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-3,3).$ \nTherefore, the $6$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}6t\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{36(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ [3{t}^{2}]_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{36(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{3}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{3})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221451 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e01d04-6c13-52eb-a4b6-ad9a5cde8134" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0ac3e0b-2daf-5d1e-beff-f97fddbb7155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316364} {:answer/id #uuid "f80c16b0-b617-5e6f-9cbf-e99c39b1f438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316504} {:answer/id #uuid "f9066d99-512e-552e-8140-af7ecdf45283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316508} {:answer/id #uuid "fe128583-dbef-5676-9904-6cbef28f082d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f80c16b0-b617-5e6f-9cbf-e99c39b1f438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})" :db/id #edb/r